        rdfs:comment                    "The saphenous vein runs reliably just anterior to medial malleolus and is large and straight. It is easy to access and lasts well although is not always readily visualised. These veins are also good sites for insertion of percutaneous central venous catheters and should again be avoided in an infant likely to need long term IV access." ;
